    "result_text": "The full suite is green: 17 tests, 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `ownerSegment` following the codebase's existing \"derived getter + util class\" pattern, keeping each piece of logic in the right place:\n\n1. **New util `OwnerSegment`** (`src/main/java/.../util/OwnerSegment.java`) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility class that owns only the classification: `of(membershipLevel, locality)` returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`, where TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`, and AREA is `METRO` when locality \u2208 {NSW, VIC, QLD} else `REGIONAL`. This mirrors the existing `AgeBand`/`RegionTimezone` utils, each of which owns its own region table.\n\n2. **Derived getter on `Owner`** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 `getOwnerSegment()` composes the existing `getMembershipLevel()` and `getLocality()` getters and delegates to `OwnerSegment.of(...)`, reusing the established locality/membership logic rather than duplicating it. Documented as \"Derived from stored state, never persisted\", consistent with its neighbours.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `readOnly` `ownerSegment` enum property (the four allowed values) to the `Owner` schema. The DTO is generated from this at build time, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name to `Owner.getOwnerSegment()` \u2014 no mapper or responder changes needed.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) and all 17 existing tests pass.",
